    [976] = {
        {
            id = 52030,
            score = 47,
            author = "HighFive",
            text = "The Tower of Althalaxx part 5 (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=973) has to be completed in order to get this quest.\n\nThis quest is pretty hard and you'll probably not be able to solo it until at least level 26. You get ambushed three times. When I'm leveling a char and try doing this quest as soon as I finish The Tower of Althalaxx part 5 (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=973) I get as far as the last ambush which consists of two spellcaster and one melee satyr. They hit pretty hard, so they'll kill you or the NPC easily(unless you're a hunter and thus can use your pet to seperate the 3 mobs on each one of you, then you might stand a chance).\n\nI suggest trying to do this quest after turning in The Tower of Althalaxx part 6 (http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=1140), which you should've done along with quests from Forrest Song and gained a level or two.",
            date = "2007-03-16T08:37:14-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=976#comments:id=52030",
        },
        {
            id = 48916,
            score = 30,
            author = "15975",
            text = "This thing really should show a group needed in the quest log.  He *says* \"if you and others act as my guards\" and he means it.  First time I tried I got to the second mob spawn, which is 3 undead scouts.  I didn't realize one of them was on the NPC instead of me and he died right as I killed the second mob.  Second time I tried, I had them all on me (level 24 druid) and killed them.  I'm on a PvP server and there had been a ?? shaman running around that had killed me earlier so we set off towards the border, I'm scanning over my shoulder hoping we'll hit friendly territory.  We do, and I start to breathe easier.  Sadly, about 5 seconds later 3 named satyr pop out, one summons an imp, they all start casting spells (2 at the NPC, the third on me as I charged him in bear) and before I had the guy at half life, the NPC was dead.  I died shortly thereafter, and about the only good news there is that I was 10 feet from the closest graveyard.  Don't do this quest without at least 2 people, maybe even 3 for the fight at the end.",
            date = "2007-03-09T23:32:25-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=976#comments:id=48916",
        },
        {
            id = 150273,
            score = 30,
            author = "Sihmm",
            text = "This quest involves escorting Feero Ironhand at normal player running-speed along the road from Maestra's Post in Ashenvale (26,38) to just over the border of Darkshore (43,94).  Feero is ambushed three times by groups of specially-spawning quest mobs, but will also stop along the way to attack any wildlife that wanders into his aggro range.  Following each attack, Feero runs back to the spot he was standing just before the ambush and says a line.  After a few seconds he starts running again - eating, drinking, looting etc for too long will render you unable to catch him up without speed increasing abilities.\n\nNote that, depending on your level and where you are standing on the road, the ambushers may aggro Feero instead of you (or your group).  If they all target him at the start he will die very quickly, so make sure to quickly get the attention of as many mobs as possible if they do aggro him to start with.  The quicker you do it, the fewer mobs you have to \"tank\" as he can quite easily survive the assault of one or two for a short time.  Similarly, if they all target you to start with, Feero will pull aggro from the one he attacks unless you also attack it or cause threat from a damage shield, heal, etc.\n\nFirst Ambush - Ashenvale, 25,30\nFeero Ironhand says: It looks like we're in trouble.  Look lively, here they come!\n4x level 21 Dark Strand Assassins (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=3879) spawn.  Regular melee mobs, will attempt to run away at low health (but will not bring adds when they do so, as there are no further adds to bring!).\nOnce they are dead, Feero Ironhand says: Assassins from that cult you found... Let's get moving before someone else finds us out here.\n\nSecond Ambush - Ashenvale, 26,23\nFeero Ironhand says: Hold!  I sense an evil presence... Undead!\nForsaken Scout says: A paladin!  Slaying him would please the master.  Attack!\n3x level 23 Forsaken Scouts (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=3893) spawn.  One of them seemed to spawn a few seconds after the other two.  Again these have no special abilities, and will attempt to run away at low health.\nOnce killed, Feero Ironhand says: They're coming out of the woodwork today. Let's keep moving or we may find more things that want me dead.\n\nFinal Ambush - Darkshore, 43,94\nFeero Ironhand says: These three again?\nBalizar the Umbrage says: Not quite so sure of yourself without the Purifier, hm?\nFeero Ironhand says: I'll finish you off for good this time!\nMeanwhile 3 level 24 named satyrs have spawned and block the path:\nLeft (West): Caedakar the Vicious (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=3900): fires lightning bolts.  Attempts to run away at low health (but will turn around and start firing lightning bolts again if not killed).  The other two satyrs do not run away (or maybe just died too quickly!).\nCentre, front: Aligar the Tormentor (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=3898): warrior-type (uses battle stance!), can hamstring.\nRight (East): Balizar the Umbrage (http://www.wowhead.com/?npc=3899): fires shadow bolts and can cast curse of agony; has an imp pet which casts firebolts.\nOn their death, Feero Ironhand says: Well done! I should be fine on my own from here. Remember to talk to Delgren when you return to Maestra's Post in Ashenvale.\nThe quest is \"complete\" at this point.  Feero then runs a little distance up the road and despawns, allowing you to run back to Maestra's Post and hand in the quest.",
            date = "2007-09-07T10:14:55-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=976#comments:id=150273",
        },
        {
            id = 135219,
            score = 18,
            author = "2717",
            text = "When I saw \"deliver messages and supplies to Sentinel Starbreeze in Auberdine\" I died a little inside..however, fear not!, He jsut wants to be taken to the border of Ashenvale, not all the way north to Auberdine,",
            date = "2007-08-10T03:22:45-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=976#comments:id=135219",
        },
        {
            id = 191421,
            score = 9,
            author = "vexis58",
            text = "I completed it with only slight difficulty as a level 26 shaman, mostly using Stoneclaw Totem to keep the mobs off of him at the beginning of the fight while I picked one or two off.\n\nAn important note here, the escort npc CAN be healed.\n\nHe only has 480 health, so my current rank of Lesser Healing wave healed a good chunk of it. Simple healing aggro kept the mobs off of him and on me for the most part after my totem died, though I did have to use a potion on the second fight because my heals were being knocked back too much for me to heal myself.\n\nThe third fight was a piece of cake, I just let him tank the warrior while I interrupted the spells of the casters with Earth Shock.",
            date = "2007-11-26T05:09:49-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=976#comments:id=191421",
        },
    },
