    [6462] = {
        {
            id = 16939,
            score = 30,
            author = "munix",
            text = "Careful in this cave, things respawn very quickly. Watch your back as you progress through it or you'll end up with respawned adds easily. The troll chests respawn quickly as well though, so you can circle around one room and finish the quest pretty quickly.",
            date = "2006-12-18T14:08:11-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=6462#comments:id=16939",
        },
        {
            id = 299411,
            score = 25,
            author = "152515_",
            text = "I didn't find it very clear how to enter the cave.... I went around the cliff face to the left of the Thistlefur camp in hope of the cave being on that bit of green where the loc is placed.\n\nIf you encounter a load of troll warlocks with imps and a few blood elfs holding tourches you have gone the wrong way.. reach 31.47 and keep going north untill you hit a cave loc 38.30",
            date = "2008-06-04T02:10:55-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=6462#comments:id=299411",
        },
        {
            id = 186636,
            score = 18,
            author = "Bury",
            text = "You can grab an escort quest in the same cave: Freedom to Ruul: http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=6482",
            date = "2007-11-17T22:48:21-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=6462#comments:id=186636",
        },
        {
            id = 361866,
            score = 11,
            author = "149175",
            text = "The entrance to the cave is at 38, 30, but you can't just get to it from any direction. Take the road from 31, 46 north up through Thistlefur Village. This is an excellent time to do the \"Between a Rock and a Thistlefur\" quest.\n\nKeep heading north, and walk up the little steep path to the northwest. There will be two more mobs here. The cave entrance is on your right. The Thistlefur mobs in here are levels 23-24.\n\nYou are looking for small brown sparkly boxes along the walls. Each one contains one troll charm. They respawn pretty quickly, so don't worry about going too far into the cave.\n\nInside the main entrance and to your left is a little trail. Go down it to pick up the quest \"Freedom to Ruul.\" WARNING: This quest should be done with a friend/group. You have to take Ruul down through most of Thistlefur Village, and he aggros mobs like crazy.",
            date = "2008-08-25T17:51:25-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=6462#comments:id=361866",
        },
        {
            id = 178361,
            score = 6,
            author = "53011",
            text = "In addition to watching your back, if you happen to go across the bridge, keep an eye below, I pulled 5 adds just by standing on the bridge when a patrol happened by. ><",
            date = "2007-11-03T00:44:27-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=6462#comments:id=178361",
        },
    },
    [6482] = {
        {
            id = 185509,
            score = 33,
            author = "45688_",
            text = "The best tactic I've found for this quest is to just point at Ruul in his cage, laugh and keep on walking.  He is so not worth the trouble.",
            date = "2007-11-16T02:19:04-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=6482#comments:id=185509",
        },
        {
            id = 142549,
            score = 30,
            author = "35072",
            text = "I'm a Druid, I love Druids, but this quest made me want to go to Moonglade and give everyone there a great big nutpunch.\n\nAs the previous comments have stated, if you intend to do this quest solo, it's all but necessary to clear the path between Ruul and the hub that splits into upper and lower paths before his room. This includes the far side of the hub (near the entrance), as those mobs are liable to add during the fight if there's an unlucky runner or Ruul gets positioned badly. Remember to get the caster furblog who paths alongside the upper ramp, as he can easily add during the scripted fights if not dealt with.\n\nThe first pack, which appears going down the upper path of the hub and will normally intercept Ruul in the hub, consists of an Avenger, Pathfinder, and Shaman. This pack is the most tricky of the entire quest. A few things to keep in mind:\n\n- Ruul can take a single furblog at a time without taking too much damage, but the furblog will eventually flee and may draw adds. So don't take your eyes off Ruul just because the given fight won't kill him.\n\n- This pack cannot be avoided by trying to stall Ruul and having them despawn before they enter combat. This pack will not despawn within a reasonable timeframe, but will rather travel to the far end of the room and simply sit there, likely on top of other mobs if the room wasn't fully cleared. This will pretty much guarantee a failed quest, and there's really no profit in trying to do so.\n\n- Let Ruul aggro the pack. No matter what. He has terrible, terrible AI and will simply walk past you if you engage the pack first, leaving you to fend with 3 mobs while he goes and fights (and possibly dies) to whatever lies ahead. If you can take these mobs out all at once, I guess that's okay, but it's not easy.\n\n- Whatever your strategy is, take the Avenger down in these packs first. Yes, the Shaman will probably get a heal off, but this is a small price to pay in order to avoid enraging him by killing another mob. He easily does half the DPS of the entire group.\n\nHopefully these tips help you get past the first pack. After that, things are relatively easy, but still not a cakewalk. Ruul will path through the furblog camp and draw adds... often several at once, which can be quite dangerous. It's advisable to clear ahead of him if you aren't near the end where the second pack of furblogs spawns. If not, remember... whatever you aggro, Ruul is liable to ignore and just keep going past. Don't get in a fight with a mob on the side while Ruul aggros 3.\n\nAt the end (past one of the gates, I forget exactly where), you have to deal with another 3-pack. Thankfully, the risk of adds is much lower this time, making the fight more managable. Beat them and you're pretty much in the clear.\n\nGood luck.",
            date = "2007-08-22T23:12:41-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=6482#comments:id=142549",
        },
        {
            id = 2871965,
            score = 23,
            author = "JasperKazai",
            text = "This quest is practically impossible for melee classes as it currently is, due to the messed up scaling on the https://www.wowhead.com/spell=6813 buff. Fighting just one Thistlefur furbolg will likely bring you down to around 50% health. This quest has a couple of spots where they spawn packs of 3 furbolgs to try and stop you. If you're a melee class, especially one without much self-healing, it's pretty much an impossible task to kill them all without dying.",
            date = "2019-02-17T16:40:12-06:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=6482#comments:id=2871965",
        },
        {
            id = 1074419,
            score = 17,
            author = "210672",
            text = "to think that Ruul can simply go cat and stealth once you leave the cage... seriously, l2p n00b!",
            date = "2010-07-06T11:14:57-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=6482#comments:id=1074419",
        },
        {
            id = 1303,
            score = 9,
            author = "4634",
            text = "This is not an easy escort quest to solo at the stated level due to the fast Thistlefur respawn rate. It is suggested to get a group together to do this quest. If everyone is level appropriate you should pre-clear to the cave entrance just prior to starting the quest.\n\nThe two other quests in this area are:\nBetween a Rock and a Thistlefur - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=216\nTroll Charm - http://www.wowhead.com/?quest=6462\n(These two should be done prior to \"Freedom to Ruul\" to speed your questing.)",
            date = "2006-10-01T17:44:34-05:00",
            sourceUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/quest=6482#comments:id=1303",
        },
    },
